Falsifies `e1000e::platform_controller_hub::physical_layer_device::proofs::a_paged_access_selects_the_offsets_own_page_and_register`.

The defect: the page bound goes back to the 16-bit page field FreeBSD masks with, so a page above
0x7ff is accepted and its select value (`page << 5`) is truncated to 16 bits. The access then lands
on a different page than the one asked for, which is what FreeBSD's `e1000_set_page_igp` does with
the same input.

Expected to fail: the select assertion, on any offset whose page is 0x800 or more.

diff --git a/crates/e1000e/src/platform_controller_hub/physical_layer_device.rs b/crates/e1000e/src/platform_controller_hub/physical_layer_device.rs
--- a/crates/e1000e/src/platform_controller_hub/physical_layer_device.rs
+++ b/crates/e1000e/src/platform_controller_hub/physical_layer_device.rs
@@ -473,7 +473,7 @@
 pub const fn plan_paged_access(offset: u32) -> Result<PagedAccessPlan, Error> {
     let page = offset >> PHYSICAL_LAYER_DEVICE_PAGE_SHIFT;
     let register = offset & MAXIMUM_PHYSICAL_LAYER_DEVICE_REGISTER_ADDRESS;
-    if page == BM_WUC_PAGE || (page > 0 && page < FIRST_PAGE_AT_ADDRESS_ONE) || page > MAXIMUM_PAGE
+    if page == BM_WUC_PAGE || (page > 0 && page < FIRST_PAGE_AT_ADDRESS_ONE) || page > 0xffff
     {
         return Err(Error::PageNotPorted);
     }
